Probing helps here.  Fleeing monsters are scared.  Of course, there
are cases in which a monster cannot move except but to hit you, so
they will.  Attacking any scared monster makes you a caitiff.  If you
know a monster is scared (which is where probing comes in handy), you
would know whether or not you can safely attack.  Not all fleeing
monsters are scared, however.  Thieves come immediately to mind,
especially non-teleporting thieves:  namely monkeys.  If a monster has
stolen from you, you may freely hunt them down and slaughter them. 
This is a very lawful action, because no truly lawful creature would
dream of robbing another creature.  Thus, they are evil (chaotic?) and
must be slaughtered (so thinks the knight).

Of course, the mitigating factor here is that there is only a -1
alignment penalty for being a caitiff.

